course: dictionary
lesson: 12387
title: Cult: a group, a passion, a fan favourite
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one you need. Look at the words around cult. «Ancient cults worshipped gods in temples.» The words ancient, gods and temples show that cult means a religious group here.
explain: Cult can be a serious warning word. «Some cults trick people and cut them off from their families.» Tricking people and cutting them off from family show that the group is dangerous. Be careful of any group that demands secrecy.
explain: Cult can also describe something loved by a small group of fans. «The cult classic film has fans who know every line.» The word classic and the fans who know every line show that cult means loved by a small group, not by everyone.
fact: «Cult» means a small religious group with unusual beliefs, often controlled by one strong leader.
fact: «Cult» can also mean great admiration for a person, thing or idea, as in «a cult of fitness».
fact: As an adjective, «cult» means loved by a small group of fans, as in «a cult film».
fact: Ancient cults were groups that worshipped gods, long before today.
fact: If a group asks you to keep secrets from your family, tell a trusted adult straight away.
exercise: «Some cults trick people and cut them off from their families.» What is a cult in this sentence? | A big family party | *A small group with unusual beliefs, led by one strong leader | A type of cake | A sport played in teams
exercise: «The cult classic film has fans who know every line.» What does cult mean here? | *Loved by a small group of fans | Very expensive | Hated by everyone | Shown in every cinema
exercise: «Ancient cults worshipped gods in temples.» Find the word that tells you the cults are very old. | worshipped | temples | *Ancient | gods
test: «The team has a cult of speed: everyone wants to be the fastest.» What does cult of speed mean? | A type of bicycle | A slow race | *Great admiration for speed | A secret meeting about speed
test: Why should you be careful of a group that demands secrecy? | It is always a fun club | Secrets are always nice | *It could be a dangerous cult that cuts people off from family | It means they are very polite
exam: «The shop has a cult of fitness, and everyone there trains daily.» What does cult mean in this sentence? | *Great admiration for fitness | A small religious group | A type of shoe | A film with fans
